Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:09:57 -0700
Subject: [Backport] CVE-2026-113093: Memory corruption in DisplayLocking

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8490475:
c-v: Harden display locking + VT interactions

This does 4 things:

- This ensures that we don't access and invalidate containers as we
  iterate them (by making a copy of the collections and iterating
  that collection)
- Calls NotifyPriorityScrollAnchorStatusChanged only if we have a layout
  object, since it would be a no-op otherwise
- avoid exposing GetTransitioningElements when we finished the
  transition
- avoids exposing pseudos to Performance API as nodes.

All of this ensures that the given test doesn't DCHECK/crash

R=futhark@chromium.org, flackr@chromium.org

